#
# Conformance case: foundation/cross-world-rigidity
# AC: foundation lowering — cross-world rigidity + anti-rigidity witness policy
#     (issue #503, Tasks 3 and 4).
#
# Positive cross-world rigidity is the fourth OntoUML discipline; it quantifies
# over PAIRS of worlds and so CANNOT be an in-world Datalog rule (the chase is
# world-local). It is evaluated by bounded closure over the finite materialized
# world set and folded back in as logic:rigidityViolation. The lint cannot express
# this — it is a Task-3-only capability.
#
# Worlds:
#   * ex:worldA — the schema world (the rigid Kind ex:Person, the anti-rigid Role
#     ex:Employee) plus instance typings: ex:alice and ex:bob are rigid Persons,
#     ex:carol is an Employee.
#   * ex:worldB — ex:alice still EXISTS (subject of ex:livesIn ex:Berlin) but is
#     NOT typed ex:Person; ex:bob IS re-typed ex:Person.
#
# Expected discipline facts:
#   * ex:alice logic:rigidityViolation ex:Person  IN ex:worldB — rigid type fails
#     to persist into a world the instance still inhabits (the headline Task-3 fact).
#   * ex:bob   — typed ex:Person in BOTH worlds → NO rigidity violation (the clean
#     rigid control).
#   * ex:carol logic:dischargeObligation ex:Employee IN ex:worldA — the anti-rigid
#     Role instantiation raises a standing witness obligation under the profile's
#     "witness-obligation" policy (the Task-4 demonstration).
# Plus the type-level lint over the schema: the anti-rigid Role ex:Employee trips
# logic:FreeRole + logic:MixIden (a Role with no rigid ancestor / zero Kind
# ancestors) — the FULL lint set, faithfully reproduced.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema puns and
# all instance typings are asserted there across ex:worldA / ex:worldB; these
# declarations are the program axioms the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/cross-world-rigidity/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: a rigid Kind and an anti-rigid Role (also asserted as world facts in input.nq).
ex:Person   a logic:Kind .
ex:Employee a logic:Role .
